The fidelity argument is settled. I changed two of the reviewer's fixes, and Sol is applying the final list.

- **Bottom bar colour:** the cure is in the app's theme file, not an override on the bar. The theme never passes five of Material's surface colours into its colour schemes, even though the app already defines them. Wiring them in also corrects about 11 dialogs, 9 dropdown menus, the date and time pickers and about 16 switches. They all show Material's default lavender today, so none of them can get worse. Sol will check this with before-and-after screenshots of the bar, one dialog, one menu and a switch, in light and dark.
- **Badge:** it stays Material's standard red. The amber existed only in the mock-up's styling, not in your theme.
- **Appearance control:** I measured the contrast. In light mode the selected fill is nearly identical to the unselected one, 1.24 to 1, and the reviewer's green swatch barely improved it. So the control becomes Material's standard segmented button, whose selected part carries a checkmark.
- **Follow-ups, listed in the report:**
  - heading colour;
  - the gold backup titles in dark mode;
  - the Import emphasis;
  - the two unused dialogs;
  - Clear All's white-on-peach text, which is hard to read (1.87 to 1). That predates this work and belongs on the clear branch or its own fix.

Two deviations from the approved mock-up go in the handoff note, so you aren't surprised. The notification area opens on the Inbox, because a notification link must land there, even though the mock-up showed Overview selected. The bar is Material's tonal bar, not flat with a hairline.

When the fixes are done, Sol re-takes all the screenshots, and I check at least one pair myself. You see screenshots after that. The other runs are unchanged.

